# Learner-generated artifacts — never committed. Mirrors the sibling Terramate
# labs. The lock files appear because verify.sh now runs
# `tofu init -backend=false` in every day-3 unit (US-C-GATE). They stay
# UNCOMMITTED for a teaching reason, not a technical one — `tofu init` records
# all-platform h1: hashes, so a committed lock would work fine in CI. The
# workshop teaches `tofu init` CREATING the lock file (Lab 03), and a
# pre-existing lock turns that first run into "Reusing previous version ...".
**/.terraform/
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.marker
.terraform.lock.hcl
